<LearnLayout
  title="Projects, Quests & Areas — Learn — cntxt"
  description="The three tiers cntxt organizes your browser work into: Area, Project, and Quest."
  path="/learn/projects-quests-areas"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Projects, Quests & Areas</h1>
  <p>
    cntxt organizes your work into three tiers. A <strong>Project</strong> is
    the persistent, window-bound workspace — opening a window opens (or
    creates) a Project. A <strong>Quest</strong> is a short-lived sub-task:
    it can stand on its own in its own window, or nest under a Project, in
    which case activating it swaps its tabs into that Project's already-open
    window. An <strong>Area</strong> is purely organizational — it just
    groups Projects together.
  </p>
  <p>
    A Project can also hold manually-saved links and notes directly, separate
    from any Quest's own tabs — see <a href="/learn/resources">Resources</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Area / Project / Quest hierarchy</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Color-coding a Project, Quest, or Area</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Multi-select + bulk move tabs between Quests/Projects</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Drag-and-drop tabs between Quests/Projects</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
